Parent: 1444

## Context
Author request (2026-11-02), first of the three principles split out of 1444:
keep scripts dependency-free using standard Python where practical, to reduce
installation failures. Prefer standard-library scripts, with justified
exceptions where a dependency materially improves reliability or capability.
State interpreter, system-tool, and service prerequisites honestly.

## Scope
Integrate the dependency default into the maintained toolkit authoring
guidance and demonstrate it on one existing scripted workflow (selected by the 1444 inventory). Inventory existing guidance first -- including dependency
management and diagnosis discipline -- and reconcile overlaps rather than
adding a parallel rule set.

## Relevant files
- rules/coding-python.md
- skills/harness-doctor/references/authoring-skills.md
- skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md (probe menu) and references/doctor-practice.md (positive control)
- tests/fixtures/harness-doctor/ (probe control fixtures)
- skills/skill-creator/SKILL.md, if present; otherwise locate its maintained source
- rules/workflow.md (diagnosis discipline)
- One existing scripted skill and its helper, selected after inventory

## Exit criteria
- [x] The maintained authoring guidance states the standard-library default,
      the justified-exception bar, and honest prerequisite statements; conflicts
      with existing environment rules are reconciled.
      Done: authoring-skills.md § Toolkit principles (310223ae, b5c1383a).
- [ ] The guidance is applied to one existing scripted workflow, identified in
      the implementation report; a toolkit-wide migration is deferred to
      separately scoped work if the inventory establishes a need.
- [ ] A harness-doctor probe (scripts/check_imports.py) verifies script imports
      by AST against sys.stdlib_module_names: JSON findings on stdout, exit 0
      (instrument, not a gate; not wired into make check), positive control
      required -- a fixture third-party import must be flagged. Third-party
      imports are allowed only through an exception list naming the script and
      its standard-library or manual route, matching the landed guidance (an
      optional specialized tool only). Dynamic imports (importlib/__import__) are a
      documented blind spot, reported unavailable, never clean.
- [ ] Run checks appropriate to changed files; regenerate generated guidance
      or catalogs only when their sources change.

## Verification
Bounded procedural walkthrough and reproducible examples for the pilot. Add
behavioral tests only where script behavior changes; do not pin prose with
wording tests or introduce a new enforcement guard merely to police the
principle. Integration work only -- not an immediate replacement of every
existing dependency.
